5. Sharding + Replication
Shards, each with its own replica set
Data + copies distributed
Shard + replica failures tolerated
Best of both worlds
Highest operational complexity
Large-scale production systems
Architecture diagrams (textual):
Single Server: Client → Server
Sharding: Client → Router → Shard1 / Shard2 / Shard3
Master-Slave: Client → Primary → Secondary1, Secondary2
Peer-to-Peer: Client ↔ Node1 ↔ Node2 ↔ Node3 (fully connected)
Sharding + Replication: Client → Router → (Shard1-RS) / (Shard2-RS) / (Shard3-RS)
